  "provenance": [
    {
      "source_type": "manufacturer-pdf",
      "source": "Topps official checklist PDF: 2019_20Topps_20Series_201_20Checklist.pdf",
      "retrieved": "2026-08-07",
      "covers": "Series 1 (#1-350) and its inserts",
      "notes": "150 Years of Professional Baseball is one 150-card insert here, 150-1 to 150-150, each card carrying a printed category: Greatest Moments, Greatest Players, Greatest Seasons, Team Uniforms or Stadiums. They are recorded as designations because Topps prints them where a designation goes, and because they are Topps' own taxonomy rather than this repo's — Series 2 promotes the first three to separate inserts with their own numbering, GP-1 to GP-50, GM-1 to GM-25 and GS-1 to GS-25, and Trading Card Database carries those as separate sets with their own parallel runs. Topps prints \"kansas City Royals\" lowercase on #195."
    },
    {
      "source_type": "manufacturer-pdf",
      "source": "Topps official checklist PDF: 2019_20Topps_20Baseball_20Series_202_20checklist_20v3.pdf",
      "retrieved": "2026-08-07",
      "covers": "Series 2 (#351-700) and its inserts",
      "notes": "Two card numbers are printed incomplete and are kept that way. This document lists \"84A- Jacob Nix\" and \"84A- Touki Toussaint\" in 1984 Topps Baseball Autographs, with nothing after the hyphen where every neighbouring row carries the player's initials — 84A-SMZ, 84A-TO, 84A-IKF. The cards are almost certainly 84A-JN and 84A-TT, and that is exactly why they are not recorded as such: rows hold what is printed, and a number nobody has seen on a card is a guess however good. The two rows are distinguishable because the row key includes the name. Fifteen sections headed AUTOGRAPH PARALLEL or AUTOGRAPH VARIATION share no card number with any other file in this set, so all fifteen are autograph checklists numbering themselves and none declares varies."
    }
  ]
}
